+ what is linux
- It is the core kernel of an operating system. Complete systems bundle the kernel with utilities and user interfaces, known as distributions (distros).

+ is linux free
- Yes. The source code is free to use, study, and change under the GNU General Public License.

+ what is a distribution
- Popular versions like Linux Mint, Ubuntu, or Fedora package the Linux kernel with apps and desktop tools.

+ will linux run on my pc
- Linux runs on almost all standard PC hardware, Intel, AMD, and ARM processors.

+ shell
- You can open the command-line interface to type commands directly to the shell.
- Type commands here to run them in the shell.
- Type commands here. You can read manuals with the "man" command.

+ terminal
@ shell

+ what is (a|the) (shell|terminal)
@ shell

+ how do i use (a|the) (shell|terminal)
@ shell

+ how do i (use|do|operate|run|drive) this
@ shell

+ what do i do
@ shell

+ how do i use (you|it|this){weight=10}
@ shell

+ how do i
- It can be hard to learn everything. Just try commands. Learn by doing!

